Sval: report a Mac on AC power as charging

The battery API reads only kIOPSIsChargingKey, which is false on a Mac that
is plugged in with a full battery, or one Optimized Battery Charging holds
below full, so a plugged-in Mac reads as running on battery. Battery Saver
turns on by itself only on battery. The power source's
kIOPSPowerSourceStateKey says whether it draws from AC, as Windows' and
UPower's battery backends already count.

diff --git a/hal/cocoa/CocoaBattery.cpp b/hal/cocoa/CocoaBattery.cpp
index 50e2c1ee46..59dc5be0a6 100644
--- a/hal/cocoa/CocoaBattery.cpp
+++ b/hal/cocoa/CocoaBattery.cpp
@@ -262,6 +262,13 @@ void MacPowerInformationService::HandleChange(void* aContext) {
     if (::CFDictionaryGetValueIfPresent(currPowerSourceDesc,
                                         CFSTR(kIOPSIsChargingKey), &cfRef)) {
       charging = ::CFBooleanGetValue((CFBooleanRef)cfRef);
+      // A full battery, or one held by Optimized Battery Charging, is not
+      // charging while the Mac is on AC power.
+      if (!charging && ::CFDictionaryGetValueIfPresent(
+                           currPowerSourceDesc,
+                           CFSTR(kIOPSPowerSourceStateKey), &cfRef)) {
+        charging = ::CFEqual(cfRef, CFSTR(kIOPSACPowerValue));
+      }
 
       // Get an estimate of how long it's going to take until we're fully
       // charged. This key is optional.
